# --- Hard privacy boundary (PRD R-P1) -------------------------------------
# Nothing under private/ is ever committed. It holds the donor .xlsx, the
# geocoded CSV with street addresses, the attender ZIP card entries, and the
# address overrides keyed on donor names.
#
# The contents are ignored, but the directory's README is tracked, so a fresh
# clone actually has a private/ directory to put the workbook into. Ignoring
# the directory itself means it does not exist after a clone, and every
# instruction that begins "put the file in private/" fails.
private/*
!private/README.md
*.xlsx
*.xls
households_geocoded.csv
attender_zips.csv

# --- Pipeline outputs ----------------------------------------------------
# These are regenerated by the scripts on every run, so tracking them means
# every local run dirties the working tree and every `git pull` conflicts.
#
# Worse than the nuisance: they are machine-specific. A run on a network that
# can reach OSRM produces routed drive times; a run on one that cannot produces
# straight-line estimates. Committing them lets a pull quietly replace somebody's
# measured numbers with somebody else's approximations, which is version control
# corrupting the data it is meant to protect.
#
# data/zip_centroids.csv and data/OVERRIDES_TEMPLATE.csv stay tracked: published
# reference geography and a template, neither of them output.
data/households_anon.json
data/attenders_anon.json
data/centroids.json
data/churches.json
data/candidate_drive.json
data/examples.json
data/isochrones.json
data/data_quality.json

# --- Caches --------------------------------------------------------------
.cache/
scripts/.cache/
__pycache__/
*.pyc
.venv/
venv/

# --- Node ----------------------------------------------------------------
node_modules/
dist/
.wrangler/
.dev.vars
*.log
.DS_Store

# generated
worker/seed.sql
web/dist/
*.tsbuildinfo
